rior margins  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue with scant thin white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior as follows  SECTION CODES  A  superior most margin  radial section  B  cavity to medial margin  C  cavity to anterior medial margin  D E  cavity and adjacent nodules  90   to medial margin  F  cavity to deep  G H  cavity to lateral margin  I J  cavity to anterior medial margin  K  fibrous tissue toward lateral margin  L  fibrous tissue to lateral deep margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm adipose tissue  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm previously blue dyed tan red rubbery lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX  1 now as M  The remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted as N  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  PAUL MICHAELS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  AWAIT KERATIN STAIN  O R  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL  EXCISION , No.
