tal  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 17 Proofread by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left Breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of attached axilla  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm skin is tan with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nipple areolar complex  There are no scars grossly identified on the skin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan to tan pink  firm nodule  which is 0 3cm from the deep margin and appears to grossly connect to a second REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan to tan pink firm mass  which grossly appears to abut the deep margin  The uninvolved parenchyma is made up of 85  dense  white  fibrous tissue and 15  tan yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  There are also multiple tan blue  cysts diffusely throughout the specimen  averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Within the axilla  12 lymph nodes range from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A   The larger mass to deep margin B   Smaller mass to deep margin C   Large and small mass communication D   Tumor E   Smaller mass to deep margin F G  Representative section medial to the tumor H   Representative section lateral to and abutting the tumor I   Biopsy site J   Nipple K   5 whole lymph nodes L   5 whole lymph nodes M   1 bisected lymph node N   1 bisected lymph node Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  PAULA ARNELL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIE