d the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Vittum  REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted for Frozen Section as FX  1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 3cm simple mastectomy specimen  which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm tan  wrinkled skin ellipse  The specimen bears a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm unremarkable  everted nipple  centrally located within an unremarkable  4 0cm in diameter areola  The specimen is received with a suture designating the 12 o clock aspect  as per the surgeon  There is a gaping defect on the anterior aspect of the specimen  at approximately 6 o clock  which is reapproximated and the specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  well circumscribed mass  with a metallic clip located within the central to lower inner quadrant of the breast  consistent with the 5 o clock aspect  This area is located 6 0cm from the nearest black inked posterior margin and 1 8cm from the skin on the anterior aspect  There is an irregular  focally nodular area of fibrous tissue located 3 0cm from the aforementioned mass  within the upper inner quadrant  at approximately the 2 o clock aspect of the specimen  This area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  and is located 3 1cm from the nearest black inked posterior margin and 2 5cm from the nearest blue inked anterior margin  A definitive 2 o clock biopsy site is not grossly identified  The remaining cut surfaces consist of white gray  rubbery fibrous tissue occupying approximately 30  of the cut surfaces  No additional masses or nodules are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted in