ts of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm piece of breast tissue with an attached ellipse of skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  There is a short silk suture at the superior margin and a long silk suture at the lateral margin  The specimen is inked  anterior designated yellow  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm poorly defined  white  firm  gritty area which involves the deep margin and comes to within 0 8cm of the inferior margin  A representative section of the deep resection margin is frozen as FS 1 and saved frozen  A representative section of the inferior resection margin is frozen as FS 3  now A  Representative serial sections from lateral to medial are submitted in B through H  with B through E being the lateral half and the remainder being the medial half  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional lateral and posterior margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue with multiple cysts up to 0 3cm  Submitted entirel