 the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is a 810 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  There is an overlying skin ellipse and nipple areola complex measuring REMOVED_DATE x 8 7cm  The axillary tail composes a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm portion of the main specimen  There is a brown oval lesion on the white tan skin which is 2 0cm in diameter  raised 0 2cm from the surface of the skin  The anterior portion of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior black  Two irregular  somewhat ill defined nodules are identified within the breast  each is white pink  firm  and distinct from the surrounding yellow tan breast parenchyma  The first lesion  lesion  1  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and is located at the 12 o clock position approximately 6 0cm from the nipple  The lesion is 0 5cm from the deep margin  and greater than 2 0cm from the remaining margins  The second lesion  lesion  2  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and is located at the 10 o clock position approximately 3 0cm from the nipple  The lesion is greater than REMOVED_DATE from all of the margins  The two lesions are separated by 5 5cm  The tissue between the 2 mass lesions is mixed firm and fatty  with no apparent tumor involvement  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of lesion  1 and underlying closest relationship to deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin  closest to lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of lesion  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue that is somewhat firm between lesion  2 and lesion  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from medial portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved tissue from lateral portion of