etts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 18 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted as FX 1  now as A  The remainder fatty tissue is entirely submitted in cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm breast biopsy specimen with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating superior aspect of the specimen  There is a localizing needle running from posterior to anterior  The specimen is inked superiorly black  inferiorly blue and laterally yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm hemorrhagic area surrounded by dense firm tissue abutting the inferior margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes C F  from posterior to anterior  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  final shave margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm fibroadipose tissue with a central cavity that opens anteriorly  There is a long stitch designating medial and a short stitch designating inferior  nipple  aspect of the specimen  The surface furthest from tumor is inked anteriorly blue and posteriorly black  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  Section Code  G I  The medial half of the specimen from superior to inferior  J L  The lateral half of the specimen from superior to inferior  Resident  LAN WANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     F